Response Codes
During Sandbox testing, the response codes below will be returned to confirm the success of the tested transaction. Alternatively, the code should indicate where a possible error occur.

Code	Description
200	Successful
500	Internal Server Error
401	Transaction Failed
408	Request Timeout
422	Insufficient Balance
USSD Push Simulation
For business initiated C2B calls, it is expected that the customer confirms the payment by entering their M-Pesa PIN code to authorise payment. The USSD Push scenario can also be tested in the Sandbox environment from your application.

Users can save 3 testing numbers in the TEST MSISDN page. When the C2B call is made, the saved number will receive a USSD Push session to confirm and enter the M-PESA PIN. Please note that once saved, the number can only be changed after 30 days.
